# LINE ENDINGS ARE PART OF THE BUILD.
#
# Windows checks out CRLF by default. Twelve spec files assert against the
# SOURCE TEXT of modules with regexes containing a literal \n -- for example
# /const measurement=MIC\.micEffectiveMeasurement\(\);\n\s*const m=.../ -- and
# every one of those fails on a CRLF working copy while passing everywhere
# else. That is what failed the Windows leg of v0.2.0, and it fails
# deterministically: no amount of re-running gets past it.
#
# Normalising the checkout is the fix rather than loosening the regexes,
# because the regexes are pinning real formatting and there are twelve of them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# text=auto detects binaries by content, but being explicit costs nothing and
# means a new asset type cannot be mangled by a bad detection.
*.glb binary
*.bin binary
*.safetensors binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.opus binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.mov binary
*.ogv binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.psd binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Shipped as-is to a shell that cares.
*.sh text eol=lf
